# Manual testing (user-owned)

The user runs verification themselves by default.

## Default

- **Do not** start dev servers (`npm run dev`, Vite, preview servers, etc.).
- **Do not** run interactive or browser-based testing on the user's behalf unless they ask.
- **Do not** assume you should click through the app, open URLs to verify UI, or poll localhost unless the user explicitly requests it.

## When to run commands

- **Build / lint / typecheck** (`npm run build`, `npm run check`, `tsc`, etc.) — OK when needed to validate a change you made.
- **Dev server / manual QA** — only when the user explicitly asks (e.g. "start the dev server", "test this in the browser", "verify in the editor").

## After making changes

- Summarize what to test and how, instead of starting servers or driving the browser yourself.
- If a check fails in CI-style commands you ran, fix or report it; do not substitute with "I'll test in the browser" unless asked.
